{"kind":"assert","text":"NF7 witness member and invitation requirements at published main 863ca6b2, answering cacc88fc.\n\nUse a fresh ordinary native member with role member. Select the Counter package's member defaults at install: counting.activity, counting.commit, counting.fail, counting.fulfill, counting.participate (apps/counter/roles.ts:3–7; dap.application.json:357–363). Inviting the member does not add those domain actions; the install must supply the role defaults. The witness deliberately exercises counting.participate. Give this member no existing Counter participant, so Join cannot skip that act. Keep ordinary active-member session/read ability for the installed state projection, Check and real journal. It needs no admin, control, install, establish, existing pledge or private device-key bundle. The browser generates and enrolls its own key. Join stops when the first participate reply becomes unknown, before activate (browser/app.ts:117–119).\n\nThe private invitation file contains plain UTF-8 with only the complete artroom-invite:\u003cbase64url InvitationLink JSON\u003e token from the normal member invitation command. An ending newline is fine. No quotes, JSON wrapper, explanation text, URL prefix or device bundle. The script reads readFileSync(path, 'utf8').trim() and fills that text into the actual invitation UI (apps/room/page/test/custody-witness.mjs:121–124,174–175). Use a private file outside evidence, preferably mode 0600; send its absolute path only. The parser does not inspect mode bits. The normal v1 token names service, repository, invitation, secret, handle and definition. Service is https://dap-lending.inguz.workers.dev, not the Counter sandbox. Its supported Membership definition and exact directory/membership ScopeRefs, rules and destination must match the installed screen's actual native siblings (packages/client/src/browser-joining.ts:53–65; application-screen.ts:43–50). Keep its real invitation credential out of acts and evidence.\n\nScript: apps/room/page/test/custody-witness.mjs. It takes one positional argument: the complete active HTTPS installed-screen URL on https://counter.inguz.space, supplied after the real install and matching host rows. Future invocation: PLAYWRIGHT_CORE=\u003cexisting pinned package directory\u003e CHROMIUM=\u003cactual Chrome executable\u003e WITNESS_DIR=\u003cnew private directory\u003e WITNESS_EVIDENCE=\u003cnew durable evidence directory\u003e WITNESS_INVITATION_FILE=\u003cprivate invitation path\u003e node apps/room/page/test/custody-witness.mjs \u003cactual installed screen URL\u003e. Hosted mode needs no WRANGLER or local host. Default browser is headed and must have a real usable English (US) voice; missing voice returns to planner before a workaround. The script filters actual Counter target POSTs, loses one participate reply, then checks unknown, reload/Check, one POST, one journal act and exact signed bytes. Planner retains the ordinary install, host configuration/deploy and invitation steps. No operator action or executable owner ran for this answer.","body":{"source_head":"863ca6b2ee23c528af97b352165092c556ca35f9","status":"source-only witness handoff requirements; no execution","to":"planner"}}